-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 6, §6.6 גמולים
-- Rewards in post-primary schools: for guiding and checking a final
-- project (6.6.1), for assessing grade-12 practical work in the
-- technological track (6.6.2), and for matriculation and final exams
-- (6.6.4) — preparing pupils, writing questionnaires, invigilating,
-- assessing, follow-up exams and the ethics committee.
-- Two reward tables these clauses cite ("הטבלה דלהלן" in 6.6.2.2, "הטבלה
-- המצ"ב" in 6.6.4) are not in the corpus text; the ministry's page links
-- them as separate documents. What they give is an input here.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common

§ `6.6 גמולים`

@desc The salary every rate of section 6.6.1.2 and 6.6.4 is computed from: the combined salary (שכר משולב) of an MA teacher at the top of the seniority scale, as in force (section 6.6.4's general note: the rates follow the agreements that update it).
DECLARE `rates basis` HAS
    `MA teacher's combined salary at top seniority` IS A NUMBER

@desc A preparation reward under section 6.6.4: weekly hours, and a percentage of the full-position combined salary by grade and seniority, whatever the position fraction. Section 6.6.4's clarification: "reward" means both.
DECLARE `preparation reward` HAS
    `reward hours`   IS A NUMBER
    `reward percent` IS A NUMBER

`no preparation reward` MEANS `preparation reward` WITH `reward hours` IS 0, `reward percent` IS 0

GIVEN r IS A `preparation reward`, share IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `preparation reward`
DECIDE `share of` r share IS
    `preparation reward` WITH
        `reward hours`   IS r's `reward hours` TIMES share
        `reward percent` IS r's `reward percent` TIMES share

DECLARE `6.6 action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the final project reward` HAS `amount paid` IS A NUMBER
    `contact the pupil directly about the project`
    `contribute to the Dafna fund for the hours above a full position`

§§ `6.6.1 גמולים לעבודת סיום`

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_1/p1 The heading of item 1 (a reward for guiding a pupil's final project); its paragraphs are encoded below.

@desc A teacher guiding a pupil's final project, as far as section 6.6.1 asks.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_1__subpara_a
DECLARE `project guidance` HAS
    `teacher is an academic with full pedagogical education` IS A BOOLEAN
    `teacher holds a permanent teaching licence`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `supervisor approved the teacher to guide the project`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc approval from the institution's supervisor
    `pupil is in grade 11 or 12`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `guided from 1 Shvat of grade 11 to 1 Shvat of the next year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc a whole school year at least
    `submitted for the Ministry's approval to exempt one matriculation exam` IS A BOOLEAN

-- §6.6.1.1א: "an academic teacher with full pedagogical education, or a
-- teacher with a permanent licence who received approval to guide from the
-- supervisor". The approval is read as a condition of the second
-- alternative only (F-6.6-a).
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_1__subpara_a
GIVEN g IS A `project guidance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the teacher may guide for the reward` g IF
       g's `teacher is an academic with full pedagogical education`
    OR (g's `teacher holds a permanent teaching licence` AND g's `supervisor approved the teacher to guide the project`)

GIVEN g IS A `project guidance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the teacher may guide, approval read as governing both` g IF
        (g's `teacher is an academic with full pedagogical education` OR g's `teacher holds a permanent teaching licence`)
    AND g's `supervisor approved the teacher to guide the project`

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_1__subpara_a akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_1__subpara_a__cls_1 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_1__subpara_a__cls_2
GIVEN g IS A `project guidance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the final project reward` g IF
        `the teacher may guide for the reward` g
    AND g's `pupil is in grade 11 or 12`
    AND g's `guided from 1 Shvat of grade 11 to 1 Shvat of the next year`
    AND g's `submitted for the Ministry's approval to exempt one matriculation exam`

-- F-6.6-a: an academic teacher with full pedagogical education whom the
-- supervisor did not approve qualifies on one reading and not the other.
`an academic teacher without the supervisor's approval` MEANS
    `project guidance` WITH
        `teacher is an academic with full pedagogical education` IS TRUE
        `teacher holds a permanent teaching licence`               IS FALSE
        `supervisor approved the teacher to guide the project`     IS FALSE
        `pupil is in grade 11 or 12`                               IS TRUE
        `guided from 1 Shvat of grade 11 to 1 Shvat of the next year` IS TRUE
        `submitted for the Ministry's approval to exempt one matriculation exam` IS TRUE

`the two readings of the approval decide differently` MEANS
    NOT (`the teacher may guide for the reward` `an academic teacher without the supervisor's approval`
         EQUALS `the teacher may guide, approval read as governing both` `an academic teacher without the supervisor's approval`)
#ASSERT `the two readings of the approval decide differently`

-- §6.6.1.1ב: the amount is what the conditions-of-service department
-- publishes from time to time; ג: the owner pays it once the Ministry
-- approves the submission. Time in school months from that approval.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_1__subpara_b akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_1__subpara_c
GIVEN g IS A `project guidance`
      `the published reward` IS A NUMBER @desc the amount the conditions-of-service department publishes from time to time
      `the Ministry approved the submission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `6.6 action`
DECIDE `paying the final project reward` g `the published reward` `the Ministry approved the submission` IS
    IF `entitled to the final project reward` g AND `the Ministry approved the submission`
    THEN PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
         MUST  `pay the final project reward` paid PROVIDED paid AT LEAST `the published reward`
         WITHIN 1
         LEST  BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 6.6.1.1ג: the owner pays the reward on the Ministry's approval of the submission"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_1__subpara_d
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `6.6 action`
DECIDE `no direct contact with the pupil` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    SHANT `contact the pupil directly about the project`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 6.6.1.1ד: contact goes through the principal"

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_2/p1 The heading of item 2 (payment for checking a final project).

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_2/p2 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_2/p3 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_2/p4 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_2/p5
GIVEN b IS A `rates basis`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `checking hour value` b IS
    b's `MA teacher's combined salary at top seniority` DIVIDED BY 96

-- §6.6.1.2's rows: 5, 4, 3 and 2 study units. No row is printed for a
-- project of 1 unit, or of more than 5 (F-6.6-b).
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_2/p6 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_2/p7 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_2/p8 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_2/p9 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_2/p10
GIVEN `study units` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `checking hours for` `study units` IS
    BRANCH IF `study units` EQUALS 5 THEN JUST 10
           IF `study units` EQUALS 4 THEN JUST 8
           IF `study units` EQUALS 3 THEN JUST 6
           IF `study units` EQUALS 2 THEN JUST 4
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_2/p6
GIVEN b IS A `rates basis`, `study units` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `pay for checking a final project` b `study units` IS
    CONSIDER `checking hours for` `study units`
    WHEN JUST h THEN JUST (`checking hour value` b TIMES h)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

`a 1-unit project has no row` MEANS
    `checking hours for` 1 EQUALS NOTHING AND `checking hours for` 6 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a 1-unit project has no row`

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1__para_2/p11
GIVEN `read the project` IS A BOOLEAN, `talked with the writer so he could defend it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the project was checked` `read the project` `talked with the writer so he could defend it` IF
    `read the project` AND `talked with the writer so he could defend it`

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1/p1 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1/p2 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1/p3 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_1/p4 The sources (אסמכתא) of section 6.6.1.

§§ `6.6.2 גמול על הערכת עבודה מעשית`

-- School years are numbered by the Hebrew year in which they begin to be
-- named: 5735 is תשל"ה.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_2__para_1 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_2__para_5
GIVEN `school year` IS A NUMBER, `the new method operates at the school` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the new assessment provisions apply` `school year` `the new method operates at the school` IF
    `school year` AT LEAST 5735 AND `the new method operates at the school`

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_2__para_1
GIVEN `school year` IS A NUMBER, `the new method operates at the school` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the old end-of-year exams, their instructors' payments and materials are due` `school year` `the new method operates at the school` IF
    NOT `the new assessment provisions apply` `school year` `the new method operates at the school`

-- §6.6.2.4: the subjects that qualify are those the binder lists under
-- "practical studies".
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_2__para_4
GIVEN `listed under practical studies in the binder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the subject qualifies for the assessment reward` `listed under practical studies in the binder` IF
    `listed under practical studies in the binder`

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_2__para_3 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_2__para_3/p2
GIVEN `pupils in the group` IS A NUMBER, `standard group size` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `share of the assessment reward` `pupils in the group` `standard group size` IS
    IF `pupils in the group` AT LEAST 60% TIMES `standard group size`
    THEN 1
    ELSE 50%

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_2__para_2
GIVEN `the table's reward for the hours` IS A NUMBER @desc the reward 6.6.2.2's table gives for the weekly hours the instructor guides the groups; the table is not in the corpus text
      `pupils in the group` IS A NUMBER
      `standard group size` IS A NUMBER @desc set by the Ministry
      `listed under practical studies in the binder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `school year` IS A NUMBER
      `the new method operates at the school` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `practical work assessment reward` `the table's reward for the hours` `pupils in the group` `standard group size` `listed under practical studies in the binder` `school year` `the new method operates at the school` IS
    IF `the new assessment provisions apply` `school year` `the new method operates at the school`
       AND `the subject qualifies for the assessment reward` `listed under practical studies in the binder`
    THEN `the table's reward for the hours` TIMES `share of the assessment reward` `pupils in the group` `standard group size`
    ELSE 0

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_2/p1 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_2/p2 The source (אסמכתא) of section 6.6.2.

§§ `6.6.4 גמולים לבחינות בגרות ולבחינות גמר`

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p1 An amendment note: the section was updated on 4.7.03.

@desc An examination, as far as section 6.6.4's definition asks.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p2
DECLARE `examination` HAS
    `on special numbered questionnaires`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `held on a special date`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `held or recognised by the Ministry's examinations department` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a unique questionnaire approved in advance`       IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p2
GIVEN e IS A `examination`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a matriculation or final exam` e IF
        e's `on special numbered questionnaires`
    AND e's `held on a special date`
    AND e's `held or recognised by the Ministry's examinations department`

-- The note: a pre-approved unique questionnaire is paid for checking the
-- notebooks only — it carries no preparation reward.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p3
GIVEN e IS A `examination`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `carries a preparation reward` e IF
    `is a matriculation or final exam` e AND NOT e's `a unique questionnaire approved in advance`

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p3
GIVEN e IS A `examination`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `carries payment for checking notebooks` e IF
    `is a matriculation or final exam` e OR e's `a unique questionnaire approved in advance`

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p4 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p5 The headings "1 גמול הכנה" and "א. כללי".

-- §6.6.4 1א(1) and the clarification below it: weekly hours on top of the
-- actual position, plus 2% of the full-position combined salary by grade
-- and seniority, whatever the position fraction.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p6 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p7 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p17
GIVEN r IS A `preparation reward`
      `full-position combined salary by grade and seniority` IS A NUMBER
      `weekly hour's value` IS A NUMBER @desc the value of a weekly hour by the teacher's grade and seniority
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `monthly value of a preparation reward` r `full-position combined salary by grade and seniority` `weekly hour's value` IS
    r's `reward hours` TIMES `weekly hour's value` PLUS r's `reward percent` TIMES `full-position combined salary by grade and seniority`

-- 1א(3): the teacher in the appropriate classes is entitled even where the
-- matriculation or official final exam is taken in grade 10 or 11 — the
-- grade it is taken in is no condition.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p11
GIVEN e IS A `examination`, `prepares the pupils for it in the appropriate classes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the preparation reward, in grades 10 and 11 too` e `prepares the pupils for it in the appropriate classes` IF
    `carries a preparation reward` e AND `prepares the pupils for it in the appropriate classes`

-- 1א(2): preparation hours inside the position, up to a full one, are part
-- of it with all social rights; those above a full position are not, and
-- carry no social rights.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p8 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p9
GIVEN `position hours without the preparation hours` IS A NUMBER, `preparation hours` IS A NUMBER, `full position hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `preparation hours that are part of the position, with all social rights` `position hours without the preparation hours` `preparation hours` `full position hours` IS
    max 0 (min `preparation hours` (`full position hours` MINUS `position hours without the preparation hours`))

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p9 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p10
GIVEN `position hours without the preparation hours` IS A NUMBER, `preparation hours` IS A NUMBER, `full position hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `preparation hours above a full position, with no social rights` `position hours without the preparation hours` `preparation hours` `full position hours` IS
    `preparation hours` MINUS `preparation hours that are part of the position, with all social rights` `position hours without the preparation hours` `preparation hours` `full position hours`

-- The note: matriculation hours above a full position are treated as
-- surplus hours, and the employer contributes to the Dafna fund for them.
-- The text sets no time for it.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p10
GIVEN `hours above a full position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `6.6 action`
DECIDE `matriculation hours above a full position are surplus hours, with Dafna` `hours above a full position` IS
    IF `hours above a full position` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `contribute to the Dafna fund for the hours above a full position`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p12 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p15 The headings of paragraph ב (subjects studied by study units) and of its (2) (rates).

-- ב(1) and the clarification: the study unit is the basis, taught by one
-- teacher; teachers who share a subject share the reward by the units each
-- teaches.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p13 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p14
GIVEN r IS A `preparation reward`, `units this teacher teaches` IS A NUMBER, `units of the subject` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `preparation reward`
DECIDE `a sharing teacher's part` r `units this teacher teaches` `units of the subject` IS
    `share of` r (`units this teacher teaches` DIVIDED BY `units of the subject`)

-- ב(2)(א): the reward for the units prepared is the attached table's,
-- which is not in the corpus text; it is an input function here.
-- ב(2)(ב): preparing a class for qualifying exams over 6 weekly hours or
-- more, the reward is at least 2 hours + 2%.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p16 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p18
GIVEN `the table's reward for` IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO `preparation reward` @desc the reward the table of 6.6.4 ב(2)(א) gives for a number of study units
      `study units` IS A NUMBER
      `weekly preparation hours of the class` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `preparation reward`
DECIDE `a class's unit-based reward` `the table's reward for` `study units` `weekly preparation hours of the class` IS
    IF `weekly preparation hours of the class` AT LEAST 6
    THEN `preparation reward` WITH
             `reward hours`   IS max ((`the table's reward for` `study units`)'s `reward hours`) 2
             `reward percent` IS max ((`the table's reward for` `study units`)'s `reward percent`) (2%)
    ELSE `the table's reward for` `study units`

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p18
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 6-hour preparation scope is tenured` IF FALSE

-- ב(2)(ג) as printed: 1–5 pupils 25%; "6–9 pupils or more" 50%; "10 pupils
-- or more" 100%. A group of 10 or more falls in two rows (F-6.6-c).
@desc A row of the group-size key of section 6.6.4 ב(2)(ג).
DECLARE `group band` HAS
    `from pupils`     IS A NUMBER
    `to pupils`       IS A NUMBER @desc 999 stands for "או יותר", with no upper bound
    `share of reward` IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p19 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p20 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p21 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p22
`the group-size key as printed` MEANS
    LIST `group band` 1  5   (25%),
         `group band` 6  999 (50%),
         `group band` 10 999 (100%)

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the shares the key gives a group of` n IS
    map (GIVEN b YIELD b's `share of reward`)
        (filter (GIVEN b YIELD n AT LEAST b's `from pupils` AND n AT MOST b's `to pupils`) `the group-size key as printed`)

`a group of 12 gets 50% and 100%` MEANS
    `the shares the key gives a group of` 12 EQUALS LIST (50%), (100%)
#ASSERT `a group of 12 gets 50% and 100%`

-- The reading adopted (F-6.6-c): "or more" in the 6–9 row adds nothing;
-- 6 to 9 pupils get 50% and 10 or more the whole reward. "The reward
-- detailed in ב above" is read as the reward under paragraph ב as a whole.
GIVEN `pupils in the group` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `share of the reward for a group of` `pupils in the group` IS
    BRANCH IF `pupils in the group` AT LEAST 10 THEN 1
           IF `pupils in the group` AT LEAST 6  THEN 50%
           IF `pupils in the group` AT LEAST 1  THEN 25%
           OTHERWISE 0

#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD `the shares the key gives a group of` n EQUALS LIST (`share of the reward for a group of` n))
            (range 1 9)

-- ב(2)(ד): pupils prepared for different numbers of units: the reward is
-- for the largest number, and it does not exceed 3 hours + 2%. "גמול זה"
-- is read as the cap of this case only.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p23 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p24
GIVEN `the table's reward for` IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO `preparation reward` @desc the reward the table of 6.6.4 ב(2)(א) gives for a number of study units
      `units the pupils were prepared for` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A `preparation reward`
DECIDE `reward for pupils at different numbers of units` `the table's reward for` `units the pupils were prepared for` IS
    CONSIDER `units the pupils were prepared for`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `no preparation reward`
    WHEN u FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        `preparation reward` WITH
            `reward hours`   IS min ((`the table's reward for` (maximum1 u rest))'s `reward hours`) 3
            `reward percent` IS min ((`the table's reward for` (maximum1 u rest))'s `reward percent`) (2%)

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p25 The heading of (3) (special provisions).

@desc The subjects with special provisions under section 6.6.4 ב(3).
DECLARE `special subject` IS ONE OF
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p26 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p27
    `Hebrew language knowledge`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p28
    `Hebrew composition`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p29
    `Hebrew literature`
    `biology oral (biotope)`
    `geography oral (geotope)`
    `environmental science ecotope or life sciences personal project`
    `Land of Israel studies oral (geotope)`

-- (3)(א): from 1.9.87 the three parts of Hebrew are each a subject of its own.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p26 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p30
GIVEN s IS A `special subject`, `the year begins on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a subject of its own` s `the year begins on` IF
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `Hebrew language knowledge` THEN `the year begins on` AT LEAST Date 1 9 1987
    WHEN `Hebrew composition`        THEN `the year begins on` AT LEAST Date 1 9 1987
    WHEN `Hebrew literature`         THEN `the year begins on` AT LEAST Date 1 9 1987
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@desc A row of an oral-exam key (sections 6.6.4 ב(3)(ב)–(ה)): pupils in the group and the weekly hours of preparation reward.
DECLARE `oral key` HAS
    `hours for 1 to 5 pupils`     IS A NUMBER
    `hours for 6 to 9 pupils`     IS A NUMBER
    `hours for 10 pupils or more` IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p31 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p32 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p33 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p34 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p35 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p36 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p37 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p38 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p39
`the biotope key` MEANS `oral key` 0.33 0.75 1.50

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p42 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p43 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p44 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p45 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p46 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p47 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p48
`the geotope key` MEANS `oral key` 0.25 0.50 1

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p51 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p52 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p53 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p54 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p55 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p56 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p57 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p58
`the ecotope key` MEANS `oral key` 0.33 0.75 1.50

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p60 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p61 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p62 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p63 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p64 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p65 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p66
`the Land of Israel geotope key` MEANS `oral key` 0.25 0.50 1

-- (ד) says its teacher gets "the same reward" as biology's and (ה) "the
-- same" as geography's; their own printed keys agree.
#ASSERT `the ecotope key` EQUALS `the biotope key`
#ASSERT `the Land of Israel geotope key` EQUALS `the geotope key`

-- The start dates: biology 1.9.87, geography 1.9.88, the ecotope
-- 11.10.2000 (printed "11.10.200"), Land of Israel 1.5.2003.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p40 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p49 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p59 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p67
GIVEN s IS A `special subject`
GIVETH A MAYBE `oral key`
DECIDE `oral key of` s IS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `biology oral (biotope)`                                        THEN JUST `the biotope key`
    WHEN `geography oral (geotope)`                                      THEN JUST `the geotope key`
    WHEN `environmental science ecotope or life sciences personal project` THEN JUST `the ecotope key`
    WHEN `Land of Israel studies oral (geotope)`                         THEN JUST `the Land of Israel geotope key`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p40 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p49 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p59 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p67
GIVEN s IS A `special subject`
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `oral key in force from` s IS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `biology oral (biotope)`                                        THEN Date 1 9 1987
    WHEN `geography oral (geotope)`                                      THEN Date 1 9 1988
    WHEN `environmental science ecotope or life sciences personal project` THEN Date 11 10 2000
    WHEN `Land of Israel studies oral (geotope)`                         THEN Date 1 5 2003
    OTHERWISE Date 1 9 1987

-- The notes to (ב) and (ג): the oral reward comes on top of the written
-- exam's preparation reward.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p41 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p50
GIVEN s IS A `special subject`, `pupils in the group` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE, `written exam's reward hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weekly preparation hours with the oral exam` s `pupils in the group` `the day` `written exam's reward hours` IS
    CONSIDER `oral key of` s
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `written exam's reward hours`
    WHEN JUST k THEN
        IF `the day` AT LEAST `oral key in force from` s
        THEN `written exam's reward hours` PLUS
             (BRANCH IF `pupils in the group` AT LEAST 10 THEN k's `hours for 10 pupils or more`
                     IF `pupils in the group` AT LEAST 6  THEN k's `hours for 6 to 9 pupils`
                     IF `pupils in the group` AT LEAST 1  THEN k's `hours for 1 to 5 pupils`
                     OTHERWISE 0)
        ELSE `written exam's reward hours`

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p68 The heading of paragraph ג (subjects not studied by study units).

-- ג1–3: final exams in vocational schools whose questionnaires state no
-- units, and grades 13–14 government final exams, are rewarded as before
-- the reform: a subject taught 1–5 weekly hours, 1 hour + 2%; 6 or more,
-- 2 hours + 2%.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p69 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p70 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p73
GIVEN `weekly hours the subject is taught` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `preparation reward`
DECIDE `reward for a subject without study units` `weekly hours the subject is taught` IS
    BRANCH IF `weekly hours the subject is taught` AT LEAST 6
           THEN `preparation reward` WITH `reward hours` IS 2, `reward percent` IS 2%
           IF `weekly hours the subject is taught` AT LEAST 1
           THEN `preparation reward` WITH `reward hours` IS 1, `reward percent` IS 2%
           OTHERWISE `no preparation reward`

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p71
GIVEN `pupils in the group` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `share for a group without study units` `pupils in the group` IS
    IF `pupils in the group` AT LEAST 10 THEN 1 ELSE 25%

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p72
GIVEN r IS A `preparation reward`, `weekly hours this teacher teaches` IS A NUMBER, `weekly hours of the subject` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `preparation reward`
DECIDE `a sharing teacher's part by hours` r `weekly hours this teacher teaches` `weekly hours of the subject` IS
    `share of` r (`weekly hours this teacher teaches` DIVIDED BY `weekly hours of the subject`)

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p74 The heading of item 2 (pay for writing and proofing a questionnaire).

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p75 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p76 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p77 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p78 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p79
GIVEN b IS A `rates basis`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `exam hour value` b IS
    b's `MA teacher's combined salary at top seniority` DIVIDED BY 96

-- ב(3): the exam's duration counts up to 8 hours.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p87
GIVEN `exam duration in hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `duration counted` `exam duration in hours` IS
    min `exam duration in hours` 8

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p80 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p81
GIVEN b IS A `rates basis`, `exam duration in hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a committee member's pay` b `exam duration in hours` IS
    `exam hour value` b TIMES 25 TIMES `duration counted` `exam duration in hours`

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p82 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p83
GIVEN b IS A `rates basis`, `exam duration in hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the committee chair's pay` b `exam duration in hours` IS
    `exam hour value` b TIMES 5 TIMES `duration counted` `exam duration in hours`

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p84 The heading "ב. הערות" of the notes that follow.

-- ב(1): a member with a doctorate is computed as the chair is.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p85
GIVEN b IS A `rates basis`, `exam duration in hours` IS A NUMBER, `has a doctorate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a member's pay` b `exam duration in hours` `has a doctorate` IS
    IF `has a doctorate`
    THEN `the committee chair's pay` b `exam duration in hours`
    ELSE `a committee member's pay` b `exam duration in hours`

-- ב(2): all the members' pay together does not exceed twice the chair's,
-- unless a member has a doctorate. Applied as printed (F-6.6-d).
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p86
GIVEN b IS A `rates basis`, `exam duration in hours` IS A NUMBER, `members with a doctorate` IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the members' pay together` b `exam duration in hours` `members with a doctorate` IS
    IF any (GIVEN d YIELD d) `members with a doctorate`
    THEN sum (map (GIVEN d YIELD `a member's pay` b `exam duration in hours` d) `members with a doctorate`)
    ELSE min (sum (map (GIVEN d YIELD `a member's pay` b `exam duration in hours` d) `members with a doctorate`))
             (2 TIMES `the committee chair's pay` b `exam duration in hours`)

-- F-6.6-d: a single ordinary member's printed pay (25 hour-values an exam
-- hour) is more than twice the chair's (5), so the cap of ב(2) binds every
-- committee without a doctor; and a member with a doctorate, "computed as
-- the chair", is paid a fifth of an ordinary member.
`a placeholder basis` MEANS `rates basis` WITH `MA teacher's combined salary at top seniority` IS 9600

`one member alone exceeds twice the chair` MEANS
        `a committee member's pay` `a placeholder basis` 3 GREATER THAN 2 TIMES `the committee chair's pay` `a placeholder basis` 3
    AND `a member's pay` `a placeholder basis` 3 TRUE LESS THAN `a member's pay` `a placeholder basis` 3 FALSE
#ASSERT `one member alone exceeds twice the chair`

-- ב(4): the authoring rates are those in force on the last day the author
-- was asked to submit the questionnaire.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p88
GIVEN `last day asked to submit` IS A DATE, `day actually submitted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the day whose rates apply to authoring` `last day asked to submit` `day actually submitted` IS
    `last day asked to submit`

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p89 The heading of item 3 (pay for invigilation).

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p90
GIVEN `hours invigilated` IS A NUMBER, `the examinations department's hourly rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `pay for invigilation` `hours invigilated` `the examinations department's hourly rate` IS
    `hours invigilated` TIMES `the examinations department's hourly rate`

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p91 The heading of item 4 (pay for assessment).

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p92 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p93 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p94 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p95
GIVEN b IS A `rates basis`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `assessment hour value` b IS
    1.65 TIMES b's `MA teacher's combined salary at top seniority` DIVIDED BY 96

-- The rate per notebook (or oral examinee) is the assessment hour value
-- over the quota of notebooks (or examinees), which the subject's
-- coordinating supervisor in the examinations department sets.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p96 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p97 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p98 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p102
GIVEN b IS A `rates basis`, `quota per hour` IS A NUMBER @desc notebooks (or oral examinees) per assessment hour, set by the subject's coordinating supervisor
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `rate per notebook or examinee` b `quota per hour` IS
    `assessment hour value` b DIVIDED BY `quota per hour`

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p99 The heading "הערות" of the notes that follow.

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p100
GIVEN b IS A `rates basis`, `quota per hour` IS A NUMBER, `oral examinees` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `pay for an oral exam` b `quota per hour` `oral examinees` IS
    max `oral examinees` 5 TIMES `rate per notebook or examinee` b `quota per hour`

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p101 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p110
GIVEN b IS A `rates basis`, `outside the home city` IS A BOOLEAN, `hours of lost time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `pay for lost time` b `outside the home city` `hours of lost time` IS
    IF `outside the home city`
    THEN 25% TIMES `assessment hour value` b TIMES `hours of lost time`
    ELSE 0

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p103 The heading of item 5 (examiners in technological-track follow-up exams).

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p104 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p105 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p106 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p107
GIVEN b IS A `rates basis`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `follow-up hour value` b IS
    1.65 TIMES b's `MA teacher's combined salary at top seniority` DIVIDED BY 96

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p108 The heading "הערות" of the notes that follow.

-- א: at most 16 hours are paid for one group's follow-up exams; ג: at the
-- rate in force on the last follow-up day.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p109 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p111
GIVEN `basis on the last follow-up day` IS A `rates basis`, `hours with the group` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `pay for a group's follow-up exams` `basis on the last follow-up day` `hours with the group` IS
    `follow-up hour value` `basis on the last follow-up day` TIMES min `hours with the group` 16

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p112 The heading of item 6 (payment to ethics committee members).

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p113
GIVEN b IS A `rates basis`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `ethics committee hour value` b IS
    1.5 TIMES `assessment hour value` b

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p114 The heading "הערה כללית".

-- The general note: the rates are updated with the agreements that update
-- the combined salary. Every rate above is computed from the `rates basis`
-- in force, so a new combined salary is a new rate.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p115
GIVEN `combined salary in force` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `rates basis`
DECIDE `the rates basis in force` `combined salary in force` IS
    `rates basis` WITH `MA teacher's combined salary at top seniority` IS `combined salary in force`

-- Examples. The basis of 9600 and every other figure are placeholders.
`a placeholder table` MEANS
    GIVEN u YIELD `preparation reward` WITH `reward hours` IS u DIVIDED BY 2, `reward percent` IS 2%

#ASSERT `checking hour value` `a placeholder basis` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `pay for checking a final project` `a placeholder basis` 5 EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `a committee member's pay` `a placeholder basis` 10 EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `the members' pay together` `a placeholder basis` 3 (LIST FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `assessment hour value` `a placeholder basis` EQUALS 165
#ASSERT `pay for an oral exam` `a placeholder basis` 3 2 EQUALS 275
#ASSERT `pay for a group's follow-up exams` `a placeholder basis` 20 EQUALS 2640
#ASSERT `ethics committee hour value` `a placeholder basis` EQUALS 247.5
#ASSERT `a class's unit-based reward` `a placeholder table` 2 8 EQUALS `preparation reward` WITH `reward hours` IS 2, `reward percent` IS 2%
#ASSERT `reward for pupils at different numbers of units` `a placeholder table` (LIST 3, 5, 4) EQUALS `preparation reward` WITH `reward hours` IS 2.5, `reward percent` IS 2%
#ASSERT `weekly preparation hours with the oral exam` `biology oral (biotope)` 7 (Date 1 9 1990) 3 EQUALS 3.75
#ASSERT `share of the assessment reward` 5 10 EQUALS 50%
#ASSERT `preparation hours above a full position, with no social rights` 22 4 24 EQUALS 2

-- The owner pays the published reward a month after the Ministry's
-- approval: fulfilled. A teacher who deals with the pupil directly:
-- the prohibition is breached.
`a qualifying guidance` MEANS
    `project guidance` WITH
        `teacher is an academic with full pedagogical education` IS TRUE
        `teacher holds a permanent teaching licence`               IS TRUE
        `supervisor approved the teacher to guide the project`     IS TRUE
        `pupil is in grade 11 or 12`                               IS TRUE
        `guided from 1 Shvat of grade 11 to 1 Shvat of the next year` IS TRUE
        `submitted for the Ministry's approval to exempt one matriculation exam` IS TRUE

#TRACE `paying the final project reward` `a qualifying guidance` 500 TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `pay the final project reward` 500 AT 1
#TRACE `no direct contact with the pupil` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `contact the pupil directly about the project` AT 2

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p116 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p117 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p118 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p119 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p120 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p121 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p122 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p123 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p124 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p125 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p126 akn:chp_6__sec_6_6__ssec_6_6_4/p127 The sources (אסמכתא) of section 6.6.4.
